  "faithful": "As there is no possible organ of choice, no choice what- ever ought to be made. If no choice is to be made, every man that pleases ought to be allowed. All this is indu- bitable. The consequences of denying any part of it are so obvious, that hardly any man, we suppose, will risk the imputations to which such a denial would justly expose him.",
  "modern": "As there is no possible organ of choice, no choice whatever ought to be made. If no choice is to be made, every man that pleases ought to be allowed. All this is indubitable. The consequences of denying any part of it are so obvious, that hardly any man, we suppose, will risk the imputations to which such a denial would justly expose him."
